\taxon{Discussion}
\title{What happens when one plane is removed?}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{For a constant scalar plaquette, translation in one direction shifts the eigenangle of the translation in the other, as in \ref{fdip-01A7}. Which parts of that calculation survive when the coefficients are operators on all the remaining sites and spin directions? In the [Wilson kernel](fdip-0153) the directional mass terms add before the sign of the operator is taken.}
